# Prove a PRIVATE value lies within a signed band [lo, hi] — revealing only the 0/1 verdict,
# never the value. This is the zero-knowledge range-membership pattern: a sensor reading is
# within spec, an age is in a bracket, a balance is within bounds — proven without disclosure.
#
# Uses the signed comparison intrinsics (slt/sle/sgt/sge, v5.94) so the band may include
# NEGATIVE bounds, and the literal bounds below (-40, 125) lower canonically (v5.95 — a
# negative literal previously mis-lowered to a wrong comparison, caught by the Third Witness).
#
#   glass prove examples/prove/signed_band.glass t=20     # -> result: 1, ACCEPT   (-40 <= 20 <= 125)
#   glass prove examples/prove/signed_band.glass t=-50    # -> result: 0, ACCEPT   (below the band)
#   glass prove examples/prove/signed_band.glass t=200    # -> result: 0, ACCEPT   (above the band)
sge(t, -40) && sle(t, 125)
